  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fatsicarpain D and ME-180 through a series of target interactions. Fatsicarpain D is implicated in targeting LoVo, a cell line that is also a target of Pygmaeocin B and Dihydrocarolic acid. Both Pygmaeocin B and Dihydrocarolic acid are known to interact with ME-180, indicating a possible pathway through which Fatsicarpain D may influence ME-180. Additionally, a more specific target of Fatsicarpain D, (1R,2S,4S,6R,7R,8S)-6-[(1R)-1-hydroxyethyl]-6-(hydroxymethyl)-1',6'-dimethoxyspiro[10-oxa-5-azatricyclo[5.3.1.04,8]undecane-2,3'-indole]-2'-one, is also shown to target ME-180. These findings collectively suggest that Fatsicarpain D may exert its effects through multiple downstream targets, ultimately influencing ME-180. The evidence is consistent across different scoring metrics, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional relationship between Fatsicarpain D and ME-180. However, the exact mechanism by which Fatsicarpain D modulates ME-180 remains to be elucidated, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
